<title>GERMANY: Bankgesellschaft sees satisfactory 1997.</title>
<headline>Bankgesellschaft sees satisfactory 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankgesellschaft Berlin AG said on Friday it expected to post a satisfactory result for 1997 and predicted risk provisions for the year would total 500 million marks ($268.1 million). ($ = 1.865 German Marks)  </p>
<p>Bankgesellschaft sees satisfactory 1997</p>
<p>That would mark a steep fall in provisions from 2.5 billion marks in 1996, when Bankgesellschaft set aside substantial reserves in a one-off measure to cover risks in its loan portfolio.</p>
<p>The bank said that in the first six months of 1997, operating profit after risk provisions rose to 635 million marks from 310 million marks. Risk provisions in the period fell to 249 million marks from 391 million.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
